From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shyalya <shyalya@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 13:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bot target values cached a pointer that outlived its unit

CalculatedValue keeps its result for up to checkInterval/2 seconds. For
UnitCalculatedValue that result is a raw Unit*. If the creature dies inside
that window, the next read follows a freed pointer.

Crash of 2026-08-06 at 12:08:

  WorldObject::GetReactionTo        Object.cpp:3469
  Unit::IsFriendlyTo                Unit.cpp:5186
  ai::AttackAction::IsTargetValid   AttackAction.cpp:223
  ai::AttackAnythingAction::Execute

IsTargetValid null-checks its target and then hands it to IsFriendlyTo. The
target came from the cached "grind target" value.

Fixing the caller would have covered one path out of many, so this sits at
the base instead: the guid is carried alongside the pointer, and a cached
read resolves through the object accessor rather than trusting what was
stored. A unit that is gone yields nullptr, which every caller already
handles - they all null-check. The calculation itself stays on its interval,
so this adds a hash lookup, not a search.

Fourteen classes derive from UnitCalculatedValue, so every target value is
covered at once.

The method bodies live in Value.cpp because PlayerbotAI is only forward
declared in the header. The interval condition is duplicated from
CalculatedValue::Get; if that changes, this has to follow.
---
diff --git a/src/modules/PlayerBots/playerbot/strategy/Value.cpp b/src/modules/PlayerBots/playerbot/strategy/Value.cpp
index c78a937..b974576 100644
--- a/src/modules/PlayerBots/playerbot/strategy/Value.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/PlayerBots/playerbot/strategy/Value.cpp
@@ -49,3 +49,33 @@ std::string GuidPositionManualSetValue::Format()
 {
     return chat->formatGuidPosition(value,bot);
 }
+
+Unit* UnitCalculatedValue::Get()
+{
+    time_t now = time(0);
+    if (!lastCheckTime ||
+        (checkInterval < 2 && (now - lastCheckTime > 0.1)) ||
+        now - lastCheckTime >= checkInterval / 2)
+    {
+        lastCheckTime = now;
+
+        auto pmo = sPerformanceMonitor.start(PERF_MON_VALUE, AiNamedObject::getName(), ai);
+        value = Calculate();
+        m_guid = value ? value->GetObjectGuid() : ObjectGuid();
+        return value;
+    }
+
+    // Cached read: resolve through the guid instead of following the old
+    // pointer. If the object is gone this cleanly yields nullptr.
+    value = m_guid.IsEmpty() ? nullptr : ai->GetUnit(m_guid);
+    return value;
+}
+
+Unit* UnitCalculatedValue::LazyGet()
+{
+    if (!lastCheckTime)
+        return Get();
+
+    value = m_guid.IsEmpty() ? nullptr : ai->GetUnit(m_guid);
+    return value;
+}
diff --git a/src/modules/PlayerBots/playerbot/strategy/Value.h b/src/modules/PlayerBots/playerbot/strategy/Value.h
index 502c496..bf15098 100644
--- a/src/modules/PlayerBots/playerbot/strategy/Value.h
+++ b/src/modules/PlayerBots/playerbot/strategy/Value.h
@@ -224,11 +224,38 @@ namespace ai
         UnitCalculatedValue(PlayerbotAI* ai, std::string name = "value", int checkInterval = 1) :
             CalculatedValue<Unit*>(ai, name, checkInterval) { this->lastCheckTime = time(0) - checkInterval / 2; }
 
+        // The base class caches its result for up to checkInterval/2 seconds.
+        // Here that result is a raw Unit* which can outlive its object: if the
+        // creature dies inside that window, the next read follows a freed
+        // pointer. Crashed exactly that way on 2026-08-06, in
+        // AttackAction::IsTargetValid via IsFriendlyTo.
+        //
+        // So the guid is carried alongside and a cached read is resolved
+        // through the object accessor instead. If the object is gone the
+        // result is nullptr, which every caller already handles - they all
+        // null-check. The calculation itself stays on its interval.
+        //
+        // The interval condition is copied from CalculatedValue::Get; if it
+        // changes there it has to be carried over here.
+        //
+        // Defined in Value.cpp: PlayerbotAI is only forward declared here.
+        Unit* Get() override;
+        Unit* LazyGet() override;
+
+        void Set(Unit* unit) override
+        {
+            this->value = unit;
+            m_guid = unit ? unit->GetObjectGuid() : ObjectGuid();
+        }
+
         virtual std::string Format() override
         {
             Unit* unit = this->Calculate();
             return unit ? unit->GetName() : "<none>";
         }
+
+    protected:
+        ObjectGuid m_guid;
     };
 
     class CDPairCalculatedValue : public CalculatedValue<CreatureDataPair const*>
